    "notes": {
        "4d7e0fc6-5a8b-4193-a249-9f5d1e8a3b74": {
            "content": "ENVIRONMENT — this flow is built for:\n- Telegram account: an apiKey account holding a bot token (service appmixer:telegram).\n- Chat: group chat id -5393771328. The bot MUST already be a member of that group.\n- Retargeting: the chat id is a literal on every Telegram component in this flow — change all of them together, or the cleanup step will target a different chat than the one under test.\n\nMANUAL STEP REQUIRED — this flow cannot complete unattended.\n1. Start the flow. MakeApiCall posts a message carrying an inline keyboard with a \"Fire E2E\" button (SendMessage has no reply_markup input, so the keyboard goes out through the generic call).\n2. PRESS THE BUTTON in Telegram.\n3. NewCallbackQuery fires, AnswerCallbackQuery acknowledges it and the prompt message is deleted. AfterAll waits 600s; with no press the flow just times out.",
            "x": 64,
            "y": 64,
            "width": 520,
            "height": 300
        }
